-- Looking a word up: the entry whose words include it.  A word the section does not define has no entry.
GIVEN word IS A STRING
GIVETH A MAYBE `Defined term`
`the entry in section 5 for the word` word MEANS
    CONSIDER filter (GIVEN d YIELD elem word (d's `the words defined`)) `the terms defined in section 5`
    WHEN EMPTY THEN NOTHING
    WHEN d FOLLOWED BY rest THEN JUST d

GIVEN word IS A STRING
GIVETH A MAYBE `Way a term is defined`
`the way section 5 defines the word` word MEANS
    CONSIDER `the entry in section 5 for the word` word
    WHEN JUST d THEN JUST (d's `how it is defined`)
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING

-- Where a meaning is given by another provision (the section, Part or Act the entry names).
GIVEN word IS A STRING
GIVETH A MAYBE STRING
`the provision that gives the meaning of the word` word MEANS
    CONSIDER `the entry in section 5 for the word` word
    WHEN JUST d THEN d's `where its meaning is given`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING

-- Whether the definition lists a thing.  A listed thing is within the word.  A thing not listed is outside it only where the
-- definition is a complete list (`means` over named things); where the definition "includes" the things listed, the section
-- does not say that other things are outside, so the answer is NOTHING.  A word the section does not define: NOTHING.
GIVEN word IS A STRING
      thing IS A STRING
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`the definition of the word lists the thing` word thing MEANS
    CONSIDER `the entry in section 5 for the word` word
    WHEN JUST d THEN
        IF elem thing (d's `what the definition lists`)
        THEN JUST TRUE
        ELSE IF d's `the list is complete` THEN JUST FALSE ELSE NOTHING
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING


-- The lead-in: the definitions apply "in this Act and every other written law".
-- src:127 | In this Act and every other written law —
@ref s 5 (src:127)
GIVEN `the words are used in this Act` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the words are used in another written law` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`a definition in section 5 applies to the words` `the words are used in this Act` `the words are used in another written law` MEANS
    `the words are used in this Act` OR `the words are used in another written law`
